@prefix bc: <https://example.org/BusinessCapabilityOntology#> .
@prefix cco: <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/> .
@prefix obo: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/> .
@prefix dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

# STATUS: PROPOSED. Do not treat these IRIs as published or adopted.
# Namespace and import-resolution configuration must be approved before release.
# Source basis: BFO 2020; CCO 2.0 Agent Ontology version 2024-11-05,
# Extended Relation, Information Entity, and Event Ontologies version 2024-11-06.
# No new object properties; no disjointness with BFO Function.
# The conceptual correlation with process types is not an OWL existential
# has-realization restriction: unrealized dispositions must remain admissible.

<https://example.org/BusinessCapabilityOntology>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://example.org/BusinessCapabilityOntology/0.1.0> ;
    owl:imports <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/AgentOntology> ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1.0 — proposed draft, not adopted"@en ;
    dct:title "Business Capability Ontology — Realist Core (draft)"@en ;
    dct:description "Companion to the Business Process Ontology. Models only internally grounded organizational dispositions; business claims and evaluations are handled in a separate ICE module."@en ;
    dct:source <https://github.com/Skreen5hot/BusinessProcessOntology> ;
    rdfs:comment "Imports use CCO ontology IRIs; deployment must resolve them to the pinned CCO 2.0 dependency closure locally. The example.org namespace is provisional."@en .

bc:BusinessCapability
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf cco:ont00000568 , obo:BFO_0000016 ;
    rdfs:label "Business Capability"@en ;
    skos:definition "An Organization Capability that is a Disposition inhering in an Organization in virtue of the material constitution of that Organization and that can be realized in Planned Acts of a specified type."@en ;
    skos:example "The internally grounded capacity of an organization to conduct strategic planning through the coordinated capacities of its members, where that grounding has been established."@en ;
    rdfs:comment """PROVISIONAL DIFFERENTIA / ADMISSION RULE:
1. Bearer: a CCO Organization (an object aggregate of agents), not a supplier network.
2. Basis: the organization members and their materially grounded coordination. A contract,
   remote vendor's equipment, or permission is not automatically part of the bearer.
3. Act index: a type of Planned Act identified in the Business Process Ontology or another
   validated CCO-compatible act ontology; legal standing or institutional success may not
   be necessary for identifying the act type that indexes this disposition.
4. Latency: a disposition need not yet have an actual realization. Accordingly this class
   has NO existential restriction on BFO 'has realization'.
5. Function: no disjointness from BFO Function is asserted; a function attribution
   requires its own independent justification.
6. Organization identity and numerical persistence of a capability over membership
   replacement are open metaphysical questions, not settled by this subclass assertion.
This draft does not promote any existing BPO capability class under this class.
See docs/ADR-002-business-capabilities.md for the review gates."""@en .
